{"acceptance_length": 5.8307692307692305, "acceptance_lengths": [5, 7, 4, 8, 1, 6, 7, 5, 2, 8, 3, 8, 1, 2, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 1, 1, 1, 8, 2, 1, 7, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 6, 8, 8, 6, 1, 8, 8, 8, 4, 3, 1, 8, 8, 8, 3, 8, 2, 5, 1, 7, 7, 7, 5, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 1], "accepted_draft_lengths": [4, 6, 3, 7, 0, 5, 6, 4, 1, 7, 2, 7, 0, 1, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 0, 0, 0, 7, 1, 0, 6, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 5, 7, 7, 5, 0, 7, 7, 7, 3, 2, 0, 7, 7, 7, 2, 7, 1, 4, 0, 6, 6, 6, 4, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 1], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 22960475136, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 22960457728, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "We are given:\n\n- A team of **4 painters**.\n- They worked **3/8 of a day** every day for **3 weeks**.\n- We are to find how many **hours of work each painter put in**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Convert weeks to days\n\nThere are **7 days in a week**, so:\n\n$$\n3 \\text{ weeks} = 3 \\times 7 = 21 \\text{ days}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find total number of workdays\n\nThey worked **3/8 of a day** each day for **21 days**:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total workdays} = 21 \\times \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{63}{8} \\text{ days}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Convert days to hours\n\nThere are **24 hours in a day**, so:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total hours} = \\frac{63}{8} \\times 24 = \\frac{63 \\times 24}{8}\n$$\n\nSimplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{63 \\times 24}{8} = 63 \\times 3 = 189 \\text{ hours}\n$$\n\nSo, the **total hours worked by all 4 painters** is **189 hours**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Find hours per painter\n\nThere are **4 painters**, so:\n\n$$\n\\text{Hours per painter} = \\frac{189}{4} = 47.25 \\text{ hours}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{47.25} \\text{ hours}\n$$\n\nEach painter put in **47.25 hours** of work.", "decode_seconds": 3.748130780644715, "draft_calls": 65, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 64, "method": "native_target_eagle3", "output_hash": "5062152d4f174ba643a79a2ee9a3030a4e2af68ee172a754d54dc898cce8dbfc", "output_tokens": 380, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes